* Waveform component reference -- the "## Example" netlist verbatim.
* No title line -- see doc-verify/const/example.cir's own comment for why.
*
* The electrical domain's four non-PWL time-varying source forms, reused as zero-input signal
* sources with the same field names/order/defaults as SPICE's SIN()/PULSE()/EXP()/SFFM():
*   SINREF  sinwave va=10 freq=1000            -> 10*sin(2*pi*1000*t): 10 at 0.25ms, -10 at 0.75ms
*   PULSEREF pulsewave v1=0 v2=10 td=0.001 tr=0.0001 tf=0.0001 pw=0.0002 per=0.001
*                                              -> 0 before td=1ms, then 10 (after the 0.1ms rise)
*   EXPREF  expwave v1=0 v2=1 td1=0 tau1=0.0001 td2=0.001 tau2=0.0001
*                                              -> rises toward 1 (1-e^(-t/0.0001)) until td2=1ms,
*                                                 then decays back toward 0
*   FMREF   sffmwave v0=0 va=1 fc=1000 mdi=0 fs=100 -> sin(2*pi*1000*t) (mdi=0: unmodulated)
* See test_waveform.py's per-form functions for the exact expected values.
SINREF kind=sinwave va=10 freq=1000
PULSEREF kind=pulsewave v1=0 v2=10 td=0.001 tr=0.0001 tf=0.0001 pw=0.0002 per=0.001
EXPREF kind=expwave v1=0 v2=1 td1=0 tau1=0.0001 td2=0.001 tau2=0.0001
FMREF kind=sffmwave v0=0 va=1 fc=1000 mdi=0 fs=100
